      "writtenOn": "2026-06-02T20:53:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In `fpsensor_test_utils.h`, you use `printk(\"Error: Invalid capture type %d\\n\", capture_type);`.\nThe production code in `fpsensor_frame_size.cc` relies on the `CPRINTF` macro for logging.\n\n* **Remediation:** For consistency across the codebase, verify if `CPRINTF` is available and appropriate to use in this test utility header. If test utilities generally use `printk` in your environment, this is fine, but standardizing logging macros prevents fragmentation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 23,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 25,
        "endChar": 16
      },
      "revId": "abb71dfeec23b342d15adb88e034246dc4e0270b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
